Spring Boot guards activation with `@ConditionalOnClass`, so the autoconfiguration simply no-ops if that jar is absent, silently producing zero coverage instead of a build failure. That's why POM inspection alone wasn't enough; I had to decompile the sources and cross-reference the only prior sibling that depends on this exact artifact.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nDecision:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"spring-boot-opentelemetry's logging.otlp package (OtlpLoggingAutoConfiguration and its gRPC/HTTP exporter customizers) references io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-exporter-otlp types that are not a declared or transitive dependency of the library's own POM. The already-merged sibling spring-boot-micrometer-tracing-opentelemetry:4.1.1 (which itself depends on spring-boot-opentelemetry) hit the identical gap for its analogous tracing-exporter customizers and required adding this exact coordinate as testImplementation to exercise them. Without it, OtlpLoggingAutoConfiguration's @ConditionalOnClass guard silently skips activation, producing near-zero coverage on that package rather than a build failure.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-exporter-otlp:1.62.0\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"Required to load and exercise OtlpLoggingAutoConfiguration, OtlpGrpcLogRecordExporterBuilderCustomizer, and OtlpHttpLogRecordExporterBuilderCustomizer in org.springframework.boot.opentelemetry.autoconfigure.logging.otlp; not pulled in by spring-boot-opentelemetry's own POM (which only declares opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-sdk:1.62.0). Version matches the library's pinned OTel SDK version and mirrors the dependency already shipped for the sibling module spring-boot-micrometer-tracing-opentelemetry:4.1.1 (PR #10608) for the same class of customizer.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Exercise the core SDK autoconfiguration (OpenTelemetrySdkAutoConfiguration, OpenTelemetryProperties, OpenTelemetryResourceAttributes) and the logging autoconfiguration (OtlpLoggingAutoConfiguration, OtlpLoggingProperties, OtlpGrpcLogRecordExporterBuilderCustomizer, OtlpHttpLogRecordExporterBuilderCustomizer, Transport) via ApplicationContextRunner + withPropertyValues under the management.opentelemetry.* and management.logging.export.otlp.* property namespaces, following the pattern already used in spring-boot-micrometer-tracing-opentelemetry's test. No environment variable or system property is required: management.opentelemetry.enabled and management.logging.export.enabled both default to enabled/match-if-missing, so the autoconfiguration activates with no external config. OpenTelemetryEnvironmentVariableEnvironmentPostProcessor can be tested by constructing a MockEnvironment/ConfigurableEnvironment directly in test code and invoking postProcessEnvironment, without needing real OS-level OTEL_* environment variables.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Do not confuse this artifact with org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-opentelemetry, which ships no class files (metadata already marks it not-for-native-image) — the issue's own title ('spring-boot-opentelemetry') is correct but the body gives no detail, so this distinction is easy to miss.\",\n    \"The docker.compose and testcontainers packages (OtlpLoggingDockerComposeConnectionDetailsFactory, GrafanaOtlpLoggingContainerConnectionDetailsFactory, OtelCollectorOltpLoggingContainerConnectionDetailsFactory) reference Docker images otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib and grafana/otel-lgtm, neither currently pinned under allowed-docker-images/. The merged sibling module left its equivalent docker.compose/testcontainers packages in allowed-packages without any live container test, so this isn't treated as blocking here either — but if a future review demands exercising these specific classes, a docker_image deterministic_setup entry for one of those images would need to be added and allow-listed first.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":15332,"type":"result","duration_ms":242193,"uuid":"a283dbbd-4894-4e7d-84a6-20fe5c199c98","ttft_stream_ms":5631,"time_to_request_ms":3347,"first_content_frame_ms":5637,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

